    "created_at": "2018-03-02T03:57:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-02T04:02:24Z",
    "body": "I remember I have tried to fix compsoedPath() for Window at\r\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/327, however it wouldn't be enough.\r\n\r\nI agree that we have to fix the standard so that we can consider non-node EventTarget nicely.\r\nBasic idea should be:\r\n-  Non-node EventTarget event.target and event.relatedTarget should be visible from anywhere.\r\n-  From Window, any node in a shadow tree shouldn't be visible. (For composedPath(), we use closed-shadow-hidden concept because a node in an open shadow tree should be visible from Window) \r\n-  From Window, any node in a document tree should be visible.\r\n\r\nIn other words, Window should behaves as if it were Document, from the visibility's perspective.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/comments/369813057/reactions",
